a79c58758ba626a830a5feb10e7610422c9","intervals":[[31,33]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/cq.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Block `--help` in the Git search allowance."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"58b13e1d8f96fd74da9dc824ef963ea91fc95f43","body":"**Bound the cleanup `stop` and `archive` calls with explicit timeouts.**\n\nThe `finally` block runs before an expired poll returns `_budget_stop()`. Its `stop` call uses the 1200-second default of `command()`. If the host stops responding, cleanup can hold the runner for up to 20 minutes after the judge budget expires. When `stop` succeeds, `archive` can add another wait of the same length.\n\nPass an explicit timeout to both calls. A timed-out `stop` does not archive the agent. The existing error path then reports that the agent may still be running. Choose the timeout to fit the expected host latency. The value `60` is an example.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            stopped = command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'stop', agent]).returncode == 0\n+            stopped = command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'stop', agent], timeout=60).returncode == 0\n```\n\n```diff\n-                if command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'archive', agent]).returncode:\n+                if command(['paseo', '--host', endpoint, 'archive', agent], timeout=60).returncode:\n```\n\n</details>","id":"93c6df739a9f70b967efb8e74222254f7aa4750bcd7daf722212ed0bde5f3a18","intervals":[[41,41]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/paseo.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Bound the cleanup `stop` and `archive` calls with explicit timeouts."}],"head":"9bbe432d7fd85833dba14f557a629d187e5ef755","head_tree":"1ecd116c4ac33bbae984033dfd03894947e6454f","input_scope":[{"blob":"4327fe1046a2b7da4239e62e697e3557f3705d08","intervals":[[1,303]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/cq.py"},{"blob":"58b13e1d8f96fd74da9dc824